Amazing — I’m so excited to help bring this celebration to life! Here are ready-to-use pieces you can copy/paste:

- X (Twitter) — "We’re celebrating a major scientific breakthrough that could benefit many after years of research — join our free, inclusive community event to learn, ask questions, and connect. RSVP: [link] • Livestream + captions • ASL & translations available #ScienceForAll #CelebratingDiscovery"  
- Instagram — "Hope in action ✨ A new scientific breakthrough that’s been years in the making may help so many — join our free, accessible celebration to hear from researchers, ask questions, and share resources. Livestream + live captions • ASL & translations • quiet space & wheelchair access. RSVP/link in bio! #ScienceForAll #CommunityCare" (use a bright event image; add alt text describing the photo)  
- LinkedIn — "We’re proud to host a public event celebrating a significant scientific advance born of years of research. This hybrid event will feature short researcher talks, an extended Q&A, community resources, and clear, accessible info for people and caregivers interested in what this means. RSVP: [link] • Livestream, captions, ASL & translations provided • Contact: [organizer email]."

Press release (plain-language, copy-ready):  
Headline: Community Celebration for New Scientific Breakthrough — Free Public Event (Dateline: City, State — [Date])  
Lead: A free, hybrid event will bring researchers, community organizations, and the public together to explain a recent scientific breakthrough and what it could mean for patients, families, and caregivers.  
Body: Include a 1–2 sentence plain-language summary that avoids medical/technical promises, an organizer quote expressing hope and commitment to accessibility, event details (date/time/location + livestream link), accessibility provisions (ASL, live captions, translations, wheelchair access, quiet room), RSVP link, partner organizations, and contact info for media. End with a short boilerplate about the host organization.

Minute-by-minute run sheet (100-minute template you can adjust):  
0:00–0:10 — Welcome, housekeeping, accessibility info, plain-language context;  
0:10–0:28 — Spotlight Talk 1 (researcher, 8 min);  
0:28–0:36 — Spotlight Talk 2 (8 min);  
0:36–0:44 — Spotlight Talk 3 (8 min);  
0:44–1:14 — Moderated live Q&A (30 min; audience + online questions; accessibility lead helps surface questions);  
1:14–1:34 — Demo/poster/networking tables (20 min; volunteers guide attendees to resources);  
1:34–1:40 — Closing, next steps, ways to get involved, resources recap; optional 20–30 min reception or follow-up breakouts. Include tech checks 60–30 min before start and designate roles: Event Lead, Tech Lead, Accessibility Coordinator, Moderator, Volunteer Coordinator, Media Liaison.

Would you like me to expand any of these into separate, fully formatted files (Instagram image text + alt text, full press release with quote placeholders, and a detailed minute-by-minute run sheet with volunteer scripts)? I’m thrilled to keep going!

Absolutely — love the energy, and congrats again, Senior Product Manager! Quick 90-day plan: 
- Days 1–30 (Listen & win): meet key stakeholders, map priorities and dependencies, audit the roadmap and metrics, and secure one visible quick win to build momentum; 
- Days 31–60 (Align & plan): define your top 3 strategic goals and success metrics, build cross-functional plans, and get stakeholder buy-in for Q4 priorities; 
- Days 61–90 (Deliver & measure): launch the highest-impact initiatives tied to your Q4 product goals, track results against KPIs, and present a 90-day outcomes review with next-quarter recommendations. 
Polished upbeat LinkedIn draft you can use: “I’m thrilled to share I’ve been promoted to Senior Product Manager! Huge thanks to my manager Sarah Lee and our amazing team — our Q4 product launch was a real milestone and I’m so grateful for the recognition. I’m energized to take on this role, continue driving impact, and excited for what’s next!” Want this shortened, more formal, or paired with hashtags and a hero image caption?

Love that—here are a few playful takes you can pick from: 
Option 1: "Hey [Name], catching up over coffee and those nostalgic stories felt so comforting—thanks for a really lovely afternoon (and for making me laugh so much)!" ; 
Option 2: "Hey [Name], coffee + old stories = instant happiness—thank you for such a delightful afternoon, can’t wait for round two!" ; 
Option 3: "Hey [Name], that coffee catch-up was the perfect nostalgia boost—consider this a big virtual hug until our next one!" 
